  {
   "reference": "Psalm 106:13",
   "status": "mined",
   "source_file": "Kulish (ukr1871) Bible text",
   "block_index": 223,
   "why": "Kulish renders 'counsel' here as «присуд» (verdict), though he uses «рада» for the same idea elsewhere (Eph 1:11, «по радї волї своєї»). The chapter turns on the word: the quotations keep Kulish's «присуд» verbatim while the prose and the chapter title use «рада». The seam is deliberate — amending Kulish silently was not an option — but a native reader may prefer it handled differently."
